# SQS Processing Patterns

## Critical Rule

**Return only failed message IDs** in `batchItemFailures`, not the entire batch. Lambda will retry only those messages.

## Handler Signature

- `SQSHandler`; return type `Promise<SQSBatchResponse>`; `return { batchItemFailures: SQSBatchItemFailure[] }` where each entry is `{ itemIdentifier: record.messageId }`

## Processing Pattern

- Parse `event.Records`; for each record parse body (JSON); validate with Zod (or similar); on success process and do not add to batchItemFailures; on catch push `{ itemIdentifier: record.messageId }` and continue (or break for FIFO)
- **Concurrent:** `Promise.all(Records.map(...))` when order does not matter
- **Sequential:** For FIFO or order-sensitive, process in loop; after first failure you may push remaining messageIds to batchItemFailures to preserve order
- Add correlationId from message envelope to logger/tracer; create X-Ray subsegment per message if needed

## Message Envelope

- Prefer envelope: `{ metadata: { correlationId }, body: payload }`; parse once, validate payload, propagate correlationId to logger and downstream

## Conventions

- Always return batchItemFailures for failed items; log total/failed/succeeded; use idempotency for state-changing work; validate message shape at entry

## Anti-Patterns

- Returning full batch on partial failure; throwing without adding to batchItemFailures; no validation of message body; ignoring correlationId

**See also:** `idempotency.mdc`, `error-handling.mdc`, `logging-setup.mdc`, `powertools-batch.mdc`
